# tags: immediate-distance max-range loop-cap short-cap fixed-point wrap half-step
# Columns (signed decimal; all 12 inputs passed by both harnesses):
#   case targetX targetY targetZ arg2 arg3 startX startY startZ dirX dirY dirZ scale -> aimX aimY aimZ
# Both assert all three signed Q16.16 output words, not internal counters. The
# C output was emitted by qemu-mipsel running the unchanged 8005E2A0.c with the
# original octagonal distance, normalization, and reciprocal-table builder.
# Independent arithmetic check: wrap products before signed >>10, wrap both
# left shifts and each traveled addition, then subtract signed step >>1 before
# normalizing. Initial index = (signed(scale << 4) < arg2) << 3. Pre-increment
# followed by while (i < 9) means nine marches from 0, one from 8 (not two).
# distance_first / range_limit / loop_cap exercise each exit for both starts;
# strict_start_boundary keeps the long budget when (scale << 4) == arg2.
# wrapped_* cover product, INT_MIN delta, cap selector, and traveled wrap.
# fire_lead* are also checked at the .NET spawn boundary. fire_direct uses a
# stationary step to measure the direct aim vector (target aim point - muzzle).
